criterion <id> returns that criterion's record. criterion --of <feature-id> returns every criterion beneath one feature, and criterion --tag <qualifier> every criterion carrying one qualifier. --json writes the matching records as JSON to standard output. An identifier no criterion declares is reported as such and exits non-zero. criterion --changed compares the current corpus against the persisted index and lists every acceptance criterion whose content hash differs, classifying each as changed, added or removed.

Usage:
  specs criterion [<id>] [flags]

Flags:
      --changed      list acceptance criteria whose content differs from the persisted index
  -h, --help         help for criterion
      --json         write the matching criterion records as JSON to standard output
      --of string    list every criterion beneath this feature
      --tag string   list every criterion carrying this qualifier

Global Flags:
      --config string   path to the repository's specs.toml (default "specs.toml")
